lvement and its location within the historic hub of LGBTQ culture and nightlife. Following a forced six-month closure due to the pandemic, the diner opened under new public health and safety guidelines in November 2020. The diner closed in March 2022."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-the-roxy-portland-oregon"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Roxy_(Portland%2C_Oregon)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["5-8 Club","dish/5-8-club"],["Altabira City Tavern","dish/altabira-city-tavern"],["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Applebee's","dish/applebee-s"],["Arby's","dish/arby-s"],["Arnold's Bar and Grill","dish/arnold-s-bar-and-grill"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Be Our Guest Restaurant","dish/be-our-guest-restaurant"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Ben's Chili Bowl","dish/ben-s-chili-bowl"],["Benjy's","dish/benjy-s"],["Besaw's","dish/besaw-s"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blackhawk (restaurant)","dish/blackhawk-restaurant"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Bobcat Bite","dish/bobcat-bite"],["Boiling Springs Tavern","dish/boiling-springs-tavern"],["Brix Tavern","dish/brix-tavern"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brown Derby","dish/brown-derby"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Busboys and Poets","dish/busboys-and-poets"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Byways Cafe","dish/byways-cafe"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["California Grill","dish/california-grill"],["Camp Washington Chili","dish/camp-washington-chili"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Carnation Cafe","dish/carnation-cafe"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"]]}]},"dish/yassa-food":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/yassa-food","n":"Yassa (food)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Senegalese cuisine","dot":"#e46a3f","intro":[["Yassa is a spicy dish prepared with onions, lemon or mustard and marinated poultry, fish, or lamb. Originally from Senegal, it has become popular throughout West Africa. Other names for chicken yassa  include yassa au poulet (in French) and yassa ganaar. The term \"yassa\" refers to the method of cooking (marinated and stewed), while \"guinar\" means chicken in Wolof, the national language of Senegal. Yassa Guinar is commonly prepared in the southern region of Casamance and across other parts of West Africa. It is one of the most iconic dishes of Senegalese cuisine and is known for its tangy, savory flavor, derived from its distinctive onion and citrus-based sauce."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-yassa-food"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yassa_(food)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Senegalese cuisine","cuisine/senegalese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Lemon","ingredient/lemon"],["Mustard (condiment)","ingredient/mustard-condiment"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"]]}]},"cookbook/the-new-mediterranean-jewish-table-old-world-recipes-for-the-modern-home":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/the-new-mediterranean-jewish-table-old-world-recipes-for-the-modern-home","n":"The New Mediterranean Jewish Table: Old World Recipes for the Modern Home","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Cookbooks","cookbooks"]],"sub":"Cookbook by Joyce Goldstein, 2016","square":true,"suggested":true,"isbn":"9780520284999","intro":[["Covers Mizrahi alongside Sephardic and Italian Jewish cooking; published by University of Californi